WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.392
Now we combine several ideas in a small analytical example.

00:00:05.392 --> 00:00:11.627
Imagine that each row represents a product and each column represents a month.

00:00:11.627 --> 00:00:16.916
The array therefore contains sales values across products and time.

00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:22.680
First, inspect the shape so you know how many products and months are represented.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.595
Then calculate totals for each product and totals for each month.

00:00:27.595 --> 00:00:34.480
Because products are rows, a row-wise calculation can tell us total sales for each product.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.525
A column-wise calculation can summarize each month.

00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:44.650
We can also use the position of the maximum value to identify the best-performing product.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.749
This example reinforces the importance of shape and axis.
